All the galaxies in our sample have robust CO(1–0) detections from V z -GAL [ 76 ] and CO spectral line energy distribution (SLED) coverage up to CO(5–4) from the NOEMA z -GAL [ 72 , 22 , Table 4 ;] . We here model their integrated dust and CO emission using TUrbulent Non-Equilibrium Radiative transfer (TUNER) framework [ 56 , 48 , 10 ] , a semi-empirical LVG model. TUNER uses a 50-component density PDF to represent the turbulent ISM density structure within an unresolved DSFG [ 61 , 42 , see e.g.,] . Its Bayesian implementation [ 33 , EMCEE ;] jointly fits the observed dust SED and CO SLED using this density PDF to infer global ISM properties by determining their posterior distributions. Table 4 : CO line fluxes used for the TUNER LVG modeling. These are adopted from the V z -GAL and z -GAL papers [ 72 , 22 , 93 , 76 ] . Category Source CO(1–0) CO(2–1) CO(3–2) CO(4–3) CO(5–4) [Jy km s − 1 {s}^{-1} ] [Jy km s − 1 {s}^{-1} ] [Jy km s − 1 {s}^{-1} ] [Jy km s − 1 {s}^{-1} ] [Jy km s − 1 {s}^{-1} ] Group-1 HeLMS-39 0.48 ± \pm 0.07 … 2.65 ± \pm 0.36 … 3.98 ± \pm 0.55 HeLMS-54 0.24 ± \pm 0.07 … 0.72 ± \pm 0.23 … … HerS-8 0.35 ± \pm 0.06 … 1.14 ± \pm 0.30 2.75 ± \pm 0.56 … HerBS-51 0.30 ± \pm 0.07 … 1.33 ± \pm 0.14 2.12 ± \pm 0.22 … HerBS-70E 0.32 ± \pm 0.09 … 1.80 ± \pm 0.50 3.40 ± \pm 0.35 … HerBS-165 0.31 ± \pm 0.07 … 0.97 ± \pm 0.25 1.49 ± \pm 0.30 … HerBS-169 0.32 ± \pm 0.08 … 1.73 ± \pm 0.18 … … Group-2 HeLMS-50 0.66 ± \pm 0.10 … 4.41 ± \pm 0.83 3.86 ± \pm 0.39 … HerBS-43a 0.37 ± \pm 0.10 … … 5.50 ± \pm 0.80 6.70 ± \pm 0.80 HerBS-43b 0.06 ± \pm 0.03 … … 1.70 ± \pm 0.34 1.50 ± \pm 0.34 HerBS-188 0.25 ± \pm 0.06 … 1.94 ± \pm 0.38 … 2.54 ± \pm 0.53 HerBS-191 a 0.18 ± \pm 0.06 … … 3.23 ± \pm 0.55 2.52 ± \pm 0.39 Notes. a Line flux integrated from the moment-0 map created using the CO(5–4) linewidth ( 761 ± 36 761\pm 36 km s -1 ) from z -GAL results [ 22 ] , as the CO(1–0) line has an extremely broad line profile with large errors in CO(1–0) FWHM (see Appendix VII.2 ). TU